{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For there is no bread.</b> Until now we thought we would enter the land and craved to eat its produce. <b>And our soul is weary.</b> A form of קצתי בחיי (I am weary of my life)." "<b>Bread.</b> The bet has a dagesh." "<b>Is worthless.</b> לוייזינט in Old French, like קלקל in ״חצי נחשת קלל״ — as it is said, ״ועינו כעין הבדולח״. Another interpretation: a term of decay/spoilage, like ״והגבעות התקלקלו״ — it does not give strength to a person."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:57.384142826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}